<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cleon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 422 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cleon was an Athenian politician who dominated the assembly after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pericles">Pericles</a> in 429 BCE and pressed for vigorous war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>. In 425 BCE he captured the Spartan troops on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sphacteria">Sphacteria</a>, near Pylos. He was killed in 422 BCE at Amphipolis, in the same battle as the Spartan general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brasidas">Brasidas</a>, and is portrayed harshly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristophanes">Aristophanes</a>.</p></div>
